  <div class="callout">
    <strong>Principle:</strong> Evals exist to make "we don't know yet" a respectable answer. Every gate above is a place where the team can honestly say "we shouldn't ship this until we've measured X" — and that's the point. Shipping fast matters, but shipping a hiring product that systematically disadvantages a demographic group, or floods recruiters with low-quality auto-generated applications, does more damage to LinkedIn's brand than a delayed launch.
  </div>

